<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo wins $120 mln Norwegian order.</title>
<headline>Daewoo wins $120 mln Norwegian order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daewoo Heavy Industries Co Ltd, a unit of South Korea's Daewoo Group, said on Tuesday it has won a $120 million order from Norway's Kvaerner Rosenberg A.S. to build the base for a North Sea gas production platform.  </p>
<p>Daewoo said the order was part of a $1 billion order by Statoil Norge A.S. to build a semi-submersible floating platform.</p>
<p>Kvaerner, which won an $880 million share of the project, would complete the platform after Daewoo delivers the base by September 1999.</p>
</text>
